WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.988
Different file categories require different handling rules.

2
00:00:03.988 --> 00:00:14.666
Images, PDFs, office documents, CSV files, spreadsheets, archives, logs, and plain text files have different processing needs and different operational risks.

3
00:00:14.666 --> 00:00:18.384
A single upload policy rarely fits every workflow well.

4
00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:24.264
Image processing should use maintained libraries, clear limits, and predictable output.

5
00:00:24.264 --> 00:00:35.010
Resizing, thumbnail generation, metadata stripping, format conversion, and dimension checks all consume resources and may behave differently across file types.

6
00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:42.850
The application should bound CPU, memory, disk, and processing time instead of assuming images are small and simple.

7
00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:47.717
Document preview, conversion, and indexing are higher-review operations.

8
00:00:47.717 --> 00:00:57.314
They often invoke complex parsers or conversion services and may generate derivatives such as previews, text extracts, or searchable metadata.

9
00:00:57.314 --> 00:01:04.140
Those derivatives need their own storage, access rules, retention expectations, and failure handling.

10
00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.196
Archive handling needs careful limits at a conceptual level.

11
00:01:08.196 --> 00:01:16.171
Review file count, extracted size, nesting depth, paths inside the archive, destination storage, and cleanup behavior.

12
00:01:16.171 --> 00:01:26.039
The application should decide whether archives are allowed at all and should process them only through a controlled workflow with resource limits.

13
00:01:26.039 --> 00:01:31.446
CSV and spreadsheet uploads are data ingestion workflows, not just file storage.

14
00:01:31.446 --> 00:01:41.246
They require schema validation, field-level validation, authorization checks, import previews, error reporting, and rollback or correction plans.

15
00:01:41.246 --> 00:01:50.167
A valid-looking spreadsheet can still contain rows the user is not allowed to import or values that do not fit the business process.

16
00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:51.519
Dependencies matter.

17
00:01:51.519 --> 00:02:06.591
Image libraries, document libraries, archive libraries, compression tools, storage SDKs, scanning integrations, and conversion services should be reviewed for maintenance, configuration, resource controls, and update paths.

18
00:02:06.591 --> 00:02:13.958
File processing safety depends heavily on the quality and configuration of the tools that handle the content.
